# Getting Started

## How to Enroll at Great Commission University of America

Begin your journey at **Great Commission University of America (GCUA)** with prayerful preparation for biblical study, spiritual growth, and Christian ministry. We encourage you to seek God's direction as you consider this commitment.

### 1. Begin with Prayer and Fasting

Spend intentional time in **prayer and, when appropriate, fasting**. Ask God to confirm your direction, clarify your calling, and guide your choice of program and timing.

### 2. Request Your Academic Evaluation

Share your education, theological training, ministry experience, and goals. GCUA will recommend a suitable program and review eligible transfer credits or ministry experience according to academic policies.

### 3. Receive Your Personalized Academic Plan

Your recommended pathway outlines degree requirements, applicable transfer credits, remaining courses, and estimated progress toward completion—so you know your plan before beginning.

### 4. Complete Your Enrollment and Registration

Complete your application and registration and submit required academic documents. After approval, you'll receive program, course, tuition, and resource information, then begin flexible studies alongside your family, church, career, and ministry responsibilities.

### 5. Study, Grow, and Complete Your Degree

Progress through your courses, completing readings, coursework, examinations, research, and other requirements with guidance throughout your studies.
